  "Question": "The smaller root of the equation\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\left(x-\\frac34\\right)\\left(x-\\frac34\\right)\\\\ &\\quad+\\left(x-\\frac34\\right) \\left(x-\\frac12\\right)=0 \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nis:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-\\dfrac34\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac58\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac34\\)",
    "E": "\\(1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Both terms contain \\(x-\\frac34\\). Factoring out this shared expression turns the equation into a product equal to zero:\n\\[\n\\left(x-\\frac34\\right)\\left[\\left(x-\\frac34\\right)+\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)\\right]=0,\n\\]\nso\n\\[\n\\left(x-\\frac34\\right)\\left(2x-\\frac54\\right)=0.\n\\]\nA product is zero exactly when at least one factor is zero. Thus the complete list of roots is\n\\[\nx=\\frac34\\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad x=\\frac58.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\frac34=\\frac68>\\frac58\\), the smaller root is \\(\\boxed{\\frac58}\\), choice C.",
